  "step_2": "The individual reports having considered all possibilities. They note that Lottery A offers half the potential gain of Lottery B but emphasize that Lottery B involves a 50% chance of gain and a 50% chance of loss. The individual explicitly states a preference for the 'sichere Entscheidung mit Gewinn zu 100%' — the safe decision with 100% chance of gain. This indicates that the individual focused on the certainty of a positive outcome in A versus the uncertainty and risk of loss in B. The justification centers on the probability of achieving a gain and the avoidance of risk, particularly the 50% risk of a loss in B.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes comparing probabilities of favorable outcomes and prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable (i.e., positive) outcome. The individual considered exactly this: the 100% probability of a gain in A versus the 50% probability of a gain in B. Their justification directly references the 100% chance of winning in A and contrasts it with the 50% risk of loss in B, indicating that the probability of a favorable outcome was central to their decision. While the individual also values certainty, their reasoning aligns closely with the core logic of the decision reason — preferring the option with higher probability of a favorable result. The emphasis on probability of gain and the rejection of equal chances of gain and loss supports the use of this reason.",
